    "text": "The amount of water produced (<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>in</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math>) in the oxidation of <math><mn>1</mn></math> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>mole</mi><mo>&#160;</mo></math>of rhombic sulphur by conc. <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></math> to a compound with the highest oxidation state of sulphur is<br />(Given data: Molar mass of water<math><mo>=</mo><mn>18</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> )"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "288",
  "solution": {
